.TH EUCLID-CLI-EAM-LIST-ACCESS-KEYS 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.33" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eam-list-access-keys \- list the logged-in user's own access keys
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli
[\fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fIURL\fR]
.B eam list-access-keys
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists the logged-in user's own access keys via the eam service's
.I list-access-keys
action. Secrets are never returned after creation - only the
\fIaccessKeyId\fR, whether it is \fIactive\fR, and its \fIcreatedAt\fR
timestamp are shown.
.PP
Self-service: any authenticated user may list their own access keys, no
administrator privileges required.
.SH OPTIONS
None.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The listing was retrieved.
.TP
.B 1
The request could not be sent, or the caller is not authenticated. If the
failure was an expired or invalid session (\fIHTTP 401\fR), the stored
credentials file is removed; run
.B euclid-cli eam login
again before retrying.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 eam list-access-keys
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eam (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-login (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-create-access-key (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-delete-access-key (1)
